--TEST--
An undeclared type argument to `Core\Program::implementing` reports once, at the type, and a loop over its result and a count of it report nothing — `rule:types/one-mistake-reports-once`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Shop {
    // `Missing` is not declared. Its error is the only one this method gives.
    // The loop and the count give no error.
    public static function count(): uint {
        var $kinds = Core\Program::implementing<Missing>();
        foreach ($kinds as var $kind) {
            string $name = $kind;
        }
        return Core\Arr::count($kinds);
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `Missing` is not declared
  --> %s:6:49
  |
6 |         var $kinds = Core\Program::implementing<Missing>();
  |                                                 ^^^^^^^ no matching declaration

error: aborting due to 1 error
